---
// /prototypes/setup/people: the People milestone, as a walk.
//
// Answers to docs/product-brief.md § 5, for this screen:
//   WHO         Dana, the tenant admin, standing the program up alone or beside
//               the account team; later, staff adding a new hire or a partner's
//               project lead.
//   DOING WHAT  Listing who gets an account at go-live, with their organization
//               and role, and deciding whether partners edit their own projects.
//   BRINGING    An annual report whose staff page names the team; a sense of
//               which partners will report on their own work.
//   OPTIMIZING  Confirming the names the report already gave over typing them;
//               one question a screen; a list the product can send as it stands.
//   PAYS FOR    dbo.Person rows (name, email, OrganizationID, role), and the
//               tenant's project stewardship preference, staff or partners.
//   LEAVES OUT  Sending invitations and authentication. See below.
//
// PEOPLE IS THE GO-LIVE LIST. The walk stages who gets an account; the product
// sends the invitations and owns sign-in, so the arrow on the last screen goes
// back to the hub and nothing leaves the browser.
//
// FOUR SCREENS, IN START'S WALK, 2026-09-23. The report's staff as tiles, one
// question over the whole cast; the people the report did not name, typed; the
// one preference, who edits projects; the roster and the arrow to the hub. The
// format is the Classifications walk's, screen for screen, with stewardship in
// the limit's place.
//
// THE ADMIN DOING SETUP ARRIVES CONFIRMED AND STAYS. Dana is on the report's
// staff page and at the keyboard. Her tile is locked pressed, neither Next nor
// "None of these" dismisses her, and the roster offers her no Remove.
//
// AN ORGANIZATION IS PICKED, NOT TYPED. A person belongs to the tenant or to a
// confirmed Organization, which is why this journey depends on organizations.
//
// STEWARDSHIP IS PROJECTFIRMA'S. Project stewardship by organization: either
// staff edit every project, or each partner organization edits the projects it
// leads. Start's "Who enters project data?" answer seeds the choice.
import SetupLayout from '../../../layouts/SetupLayout.astro';
import Firma2SetupStepper from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-stepper.astro';
import Firma2SetupPeoplePicker from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-people-picker.astro';
import Firma2SetupPeopleAdd from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-people-add.astro';
import Firma2SetupPeopleStewardship from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-people-stewardship.astro';
import Firma2SetupPeopleRoster from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-people-roster.astro';
import EsaBadge from '@esa/ecology/esa-badge.astro';

const stepIds = ['suggested', 'add', 'stewardship', 'review'];
---
<!-- manifest:
  layout: stack(2xl)
  sections:
    - status counts  -> esa-badge   (two, slotted into the milestone band SetupLayout renders)
    - walk           -> firma2-setup-stepper
      - suggested      -> firma2-setup-people-picker
      - add            -> firma2-setup-people-add
      - stewardship    -> firma2-setup-people-stewardship
      - review         -> firma2-setup-people-roster
-->
<SetupLayout title="People" width="wide" milestone="people">
  <!-- The counts the screens produce, at the top of the page. Synced by the
       script below from the same draft the screens read. -->
  <span slot="status" data-part="confirmed-count"><EsaBadge value="0 confirmed" variant="secondary" size="sm" /></span>
  <span slot="status" data-part="review-count"><EsaBadge value="0 to review" variant="secondary" size="sm" /></span>

  <Firma2SetupStepper stepIds={stepIds}>
    <Firma2SetupPeoplePicker />
    <Firma2SetupPeopleAdd />
    <Firma2SetupPeopleStewardship />
    <Firma2SetupPeopleRoster />
  </Firma2SetupStepper>
</SetupLayout>

<script>
  import { listPeople } from '../../../lib/setup-draft';

  const confirmedBadge = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-part="confirmed-count"] .esa-badge__text');
  const reviewBadge = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-part="review-count"] .esa-badge__text');

  const sync = (): void => {
    const records = listPeople();
    const confirmed = records.filter((record) => record.status === 'confirmed').length;
    const toReview = records.filter((record) => record.status === 'suggested').length;

    if (confirmedBadge) confirmedBadge.textContent = `${confirmed} confirmed`;
    if (reviewBadge) reviewBadge.textContent = `${toReview} to review`;
  };

  document.addEventListener('setup-draft-change', sync);
  sync();
</script>
